0 Ribbed hoses form a tall arch, a low U-shaped return and two straight comparison lengths.
0 Name: TECHNIC_RIBBED_HOSE-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Blue and yellow spans meet at the crown of the arch above two small supports. A brown hose turns back near a pin-bearing brick, while orange and purple lengths lie alongside.
0 // Rigid construction: 2460 tiles with pins and 4730 pin-bearing bricks provide distinct anchoring contexts. A separate 3673 pin appears near the arch base.
0 // Build lesson: Use repeated ribs as a restrained industrial texture for ducts, machine guards or service loops, with visible rigid supports at the endpoints.
0 // Reuse: Two rendered spans touching at the arch crown do not establish a connector. Verify the actual end fit and support of each span before treating the arch as one buildable hose.
